-- title:
--   Seventh-power bound for the wanted reporter’s numeric allowance
-- statement:
--   For natural $n$, let $m=\operatorname{inputBits}(n)$, $h=\operatorname{microHalf}(m)$, $J=\operatorname{blockCount}(m)$, $M=2^{2048(m+1)}$, and $W=512hJ$. Choose natural bounds $K,N,N_B,N_C$ with $K\le J$, $N\le3M^3$, and $N_B,N_C\le n$. Let $R=(\operatorname{scheduleSize}(h)\operatorname{localBucketCap}(h)^2)^J$ be the representation cap.
--   Put $G=\binom{2h}{h}$. The numeric allowance is the explicit sum
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   V={}&NN_B+NN_BN_C+NN_BN_CR+J+512h+K\\
--   &+N+N_B+N_C+R+G+2hJ+1024\\
--   \le{}&100(M+1)^7.
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--   Here $V=\operatorname{wantedNumeric}(h,J,K,N,N_B,N_C)$.
--
--   The three cardinality bounds account for input products and represented raw mass; the other summands cover dimensions and control values. This supplies the numeric part of the relative wanted-buffer allocation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsWantedScales.lean#L57-L86

